t.py\nlinked-v9-0710-request.txt\nmutants.log\nmutants.py\nprefix-v119.log\npreflight.log\nreading-rule.md\nrebuild-control.log\nrebuild_control.py\nround10-brief.md\nround2-brief.md\nround3-brief.md\nround4-brief.md\nround5-brief.md\nround6-brief.md\nround7-brief.md\nround8-brief.md\nround9-brief.md\nselection-census.md\nselection_census.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10439,10453p'; nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '1,40p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10439,10453p'; nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '1,40p'\"","aggregated_output":" 10439\t## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n 10440\t\n 10441\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-21), replying to the three choices of D693: \"A\". The options were:\n 10442\t  - **A**, recommended: (a) a chosen reading link leaves evidence filing alone (D265 applies only to a stated hierarchy); (b) open new\n 10443\t    matching and judging versions for the shared mechanism (both opening orders; the first test accepts only the existing-reader /\n 10444\t    new-target case); (c) after the $0 proof has passed the council, the July comparison (old-2, 07-10 to 07-12, three linked and three\n 10445\t    control sequences, both questions fresh, pass rule `dependency-design/codex-r2.md` §7(b)), cap $0.15, estimate $0.06–0.07;\n 10446\t  - **B**, the code and the $0 proof only, asking again before the paid test;\n 10447\t  - **C**, not now.\n 10448\t- **Decided (Alex):** A. poc-v118 stays the product and the control; the linking version is a new configuration. The sourced-reference\n 10449\t  change is not opened (it returns after the July measurement, D693).\n 10450\t- **Next:** the $0 work of D693 in order (tables and request audit; the July control rebuilt by request identity and filing replayed;\n 10451\t  real checks and writer with fixed answers for both orders and the listed events; built requests inspected, rule frozen, cap set),\n 10452\t  then the council on the proof, then the send.\n 10453\t\n     1\t# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n     2\t\n     3\t> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n     4\t> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n     5\t> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n     6\t> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n     7\t> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n     8\t> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n     9\t> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n    10\t> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n    11\t\n    12\t## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n    13\t\n    14\tBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n    15\t\n    16\t1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n    17\t2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n    18\t3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n    19\t   word for it is already given.\n    20\t4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n    21\t   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n    22\t5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n    23\t   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n    24\t\n    25\t## 1. Goal (end to end)\n    26\t\n    27\tEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\n    28\tnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\n    29\tany one step's own score.\n    30\t\n    31\t## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n    32\t\n    33\t**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n    34\t\n    35\tThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n    36\t\n    37\t- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n    38\t  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n    39\t  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n    40\t  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c 'import importlib.util\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py\\\")\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\\\"july_review\\\",p)\nh=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(h)\nh.bounds()\nh.price()'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c 'import importlib.util\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py\\\")\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\\\"july_review\\\",p)\nh=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(h)\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom threading import Event\nwaiting=Event()\nproceed=Event()\nforwarded=[]\nlatch=h.Latch()\nscope=h.JudgingScope(lambda *args: forwarded.append(h.judged_view(args[-1])),latch)\noriginal=h.judged_view\ndef hold_target(req):\n    name=original(req)\n    if name==\\\"v9\\\":\n        waiting.set()\n        if not proceed.wait(2):\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"fixture timed out\\\")\n    return name\nh.judged_view=hold_target\ndef req(view):\n    return {\\\"messages\\\":[{\\\"content\\\":f\\\"Thesis {view} (fixture)\\\"}]}\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=2) as pool:\n    v9=pool.submit(scope,\\\"openai\\\",req(\\\"v9\\\"))\n    assert waiting.wait(2)\n    try:\n        scope(\\\"openai\\\",req(\\\"v8\\\"))\n    except h.Stop:\n        print(\\\"Latch closed:\\\", latch.reason)\n    finally:\n        proceed.set()\n    v9.result(timeout=2)\nprint(\\\"Forwarded after the refusal:\\\",forwarded)'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c 'import importlib.util\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py\\\")\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\\\"july_review\\\",p)\nh=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(h)\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom threading import Event\nwaiting=Event()\nproceed=Event()\nforwarded=[]\nlatch=h.Latch()\nscope=h.JudgingScope(lambda *args: forwarded.append(h.judged_view(args[-1])),latch)\noriginal=h.judged_view\ndef hold_target(req):\n    name=original(req)\n    if name==\\\"v9\\\":\n        waiting.set()\n        if not proceed.wait(2):\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"fixture timed out\\\")\n    return name\nh.judged_view=hold_target\ndef req(view):\n    return {\\\"messages\\\":[{\\\"content\\\":f\\\"Thesis {view} (fixture)\\\"}]}\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=2) as pool:\n    v9=pool.submit(scope,\\\"openai\\\",req(\\\"v9\\\"))\n    assert waiting.wait(2)\n    try:\n        scope(\\\"openai\\\",req(\\\"v8\\\"))\n    except h.Stop:\n        print(\\\"Latch closed:\\\", latch.reason)\n    finally:\n        proceed.set()\n    v9.result(timeout=2)\nprint(\\\"Forwarded after the refusal:\\\",forwarded)'\"","aggregated_output":"Latch closed: unapproved request in judging (thesis v8): not sent\nForwarded after the refusal: ['v9']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
