{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The July send is **not ready**. The revised dry run shows that Data Center reads the same day’s total-revenue answer. Two spending safeguards still have gaps, and the launcher can end the comparison before the frozen rule can be applied.\n\n## Blocking findings\n\n1. **The $0.15 cap still depends on an estimate.** I reran `bounds` and reproduced the largest historical settlement at 30.34% of its reservation. I also exercised the unchanged `BudgetTransport` with a fake provider response. Starting at $0.140 spent, it granted a $0.00863 reservation, settled $0.01210, and stopped at **$0.15210**. The census shows historical headroom. The live transport still checks for an overrun after the call. Use verified pre-send charge bounds for each Luna attempt and the full Jev retry bundle, or ask Alex to approve an estimate-based limit. I reproduced **$0.0849** for six sequences as a planning estimate. [D694](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10439) · [Historical census and price](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:405) · [Reservation and settlement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:131)\n\n2. **The latch still lets an attempt start after a refusal.** I paused v9 after `Latch.check()` but before it entered the inner transport. I then let v8 close the latch. When v9 resumed, it still reached the inner transport. The replay test establishes that v8 itself is refused and that later days are skipped. Couple attempt admission to the latch under the same lock, check it again for retries, and add a deterministic two-worker test for this ordering. Attempts already admitted may finish. [Latch and judging scope](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:56) · [Refusal test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:302) · [Budget retry loop](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:268)\n\n3. **The launcher treats one unusable sequence as the end of the comparison.** An out-of-pair link in `linked-1` stops the entire send even though `linked-2` and `linked-3` could still supply the two comparable linked sequences the frozen rule allows. Keep that sequence stopped and record it as incomparable. Continue the remaining independent sequences while the shared budget permits, or obtain approval to change the registered stop rule. [Send loop](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:490) · [Test plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:60) · [Frozen reading rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md:16)\n\n## Verified and nonblocking\n\n- The prefix check now verifies July 9 and the fields in the proved comparison. The preflight log records its skipped matching row. The saved July 10 request shows the separate v14 comparison point and forecast, and the revised dry-run log checks the previous-answer chain and the out-of-pair stop before any judge attempt or later handover. The selection code now retains the earlier call ID, identifies the failing request hash and marks later jobs as unasked. I reviewed the recorded suite and mutant results without rerunning them. [Proof table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/PROOF.md:10) · [Saved request](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/linked-v9-0710-request.txt:170) · [Selection failure record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:178)\n- Tighten the new rollback test by asserting the database state immediately after `WriteConflict`, before the test calls `conn.rollback()`. That will prove the writer’s savepoint performed the rollback. Describe the final summary as covering normal exits and Python exceptions. An abrupt process kill leaves the start log and ledger for inspection. [Rollback test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_links.py:278) · [Final summary](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:479)\n\n**NOT READY**"}}
